# The voyage itself: wonder, home, ship life, the dark, the approach.
# Arc, threads and plants: content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.
# Personal threads: each `who ow_*` opener casts a different astronaut (`!is`), and
# that astronaut carries the thread to its payoff and epilogue line.

# --- Leaving -------------------------------------------------------------------
card p_live_call
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 1 1
roles A
text {A} calls home while the delay is still under a second. Someone tells a bad joke and {A} laughs on the beat, in real time, with everyone at the table. Afterwards {A} writes down who was there and what they ate, and folds the list into a flight-suit pocket.
do who ow_list A
do mark t_call
do morale A 5

card p_music
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 2 2
roles A
when !is A ow_list
text {A} plays the same four bars on a travel guitar at the end of every watch, into the fleet channel, never the rest of the song. By the end of the week six ships are guessing at the fifth bar, six different ways.
do who ow_song A
do trait A warm 1

card l_reboot
type beat
cat life
clue core
due
once
days 3 9
roles A
text The galley screen on {A}'s ship takes a 2.3-gigabyte update overnight and restarts at breakfast: the logo, a progress bar, the three-note chime, all over before {A} has counted to eleven. By the end of the week the whole fleet is humming the chime.
do morale A 1

card p_garden_plant
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 4 4
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
text {A} plants the garden: six seed pods in a tray the size of a laptop, under a lamp the colour of a plum. {A} labels each pod in tiny capitals and says good night to them on an open channel. Several people say good night back.
do who ow_garden A
do var garden 1

card l_manifest
type beat
cat life
clue core
due
once
days 5 9
roles A
text {A} reads the arrival manifest. Habitat on Cargo 1, water on Cargo 3, the rover on Cargo 4. Cargo 2, the last one down, gets one line between a spare drill bit and a pallet of nitrogen: "lost on landing, written off". The relay list ends with a third orbiter in grey: "retired, thruster stuck open".
do trait A curious 1

card l_departure
type beat
cat wonder
due
once
days 6 6
roles A
text The last tanker undocks at dawn. Seven ships light their engines for the departure burn, and {A} feels weight come back for the first time since launch. When the engines stop, Earth is already shrinking, and by the next day {A} can hide it behind a thumb.
do morale A 3

card l_transfer
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 7 7
roles A
text The ships hold formation a few hundred metres apart. Every fifth day they close up for a transfer window: a tethered line between hatches, a morning on oxygen before it, paid for in propellant, so nobody crosses for fun. An empty ship flies itself. {A} rides it first and calls it "educational".
do trait A brave 2

card l_handshake
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 12 20
roles A
when !is A ow_list
text The galley screen on {A}'s ship has started to sulk: after every restart it sits on its logo a little longer than it used to, then boots with a sad cloud icon and the word OFFLINE. {A} files a ticket titled "manners".
do morale A 1

# --- Thread: the list ------------------------------------------------------------
card p_list_letter
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 18 19
roles A
when is A ow_list
text The delay has turned calls into letters. {A} records one for home and stops halfway, because there's no one to interrupt. {A} starts again and leaves pauses in it, where the laughs would have been. The list from the first call is still in the pocket.
do morale A 2
do trait A warm 2

card p_packer_note
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 16 17
roles A
when !is A ow_list
text A voice note from the Starbase loading crew turns up in {A}'s data drop, forty seconds long, recorded on a forklift by the sound of it. The one with the Sharpie: "Eat the good rations first. The bad ones keep." {A} checks the locker. It's true.
do morale A 2

card g_news
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 27 28
roles A
when is A ow_list
text A message from home for {A}: a funeral, already over. One of the names on the list from the first call. By the time the message arrived, the people in the photos had gone home and changed their clothes. {A} watches the recording to the end and asks for the next watch.
do morale A -8
do trait A warm 3

card c_list
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 35 36
roles A
when is A ow_list
text {A} copies the list from the first call into the entry log, name by name, and reaches the end feeling it's short. It is: the person who held the phone up that night never made it onto the list, because they were holding the phone. {A} adds them at the top.
do morale A 3

card a_list
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when is A ow_list
text {A} writes to every name on the list from the first call, one more to the name that isn't there any more, and a last one to a loading bay at Starbase. Each will land ten minutes after it's sent. "No pauses this time," {A} says, and leaves them out.
do morale A 3

# --- Thread: the song ------------------------------------------------------------
card p_song_ask
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 21 22
roles A B
when is A ow_song
text On the night {B} finally asks about the four bars, {A} says the rest of the song belongs to someone at home and gets played when there's a planet under it again. {B} says that's a deal, and starts humming a made-up fifth bar on purpose.
do bond A B 5
do bond B A 3

card c_song
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 36 37
roles A
when is A ow_song
text Alone, with the channel off, {A} plays past the four bars for the first time since Starbase and gets the fifth one wrong. Then wrong again, differently. {A} puts the guitar back in its bag. "Not yet," {A} tells the empty cabin. "Entry morning."
do trait A warm 1

card a_song
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when is A ow_song
text On the morning of entry, with a planet under the fleet again, {A} plays the song all the way through on the fleet channel, past the four bars, for the first time since Starbase. Six ships hear the fifth bar at last. It isn't what any of them guessed. "That's the one," {A} says.
do morale A 5

# --- Thread: the garden ------------------------------------------------------------
card p_garden_tend
type beat
cat life
once
days 8 20
weight 10
roles A
when is A ow_garden
text {A} waters the garden tray with a syringe, two millilitres per pod, and checks each one under the lamp. Nothing yet. {A} logs the nothing as carefully as anything else.
do var garden 1

card p_garden_fail
type beat
cat grim
due
once
days 18 19
roles A
when is A ow_garden
text Four of the six pods have gone soft and grey: drowned. The schedule came from a book written for windowsills, where water drains away. Up here it just sits. {A} lifts them out with tweezers. "My fault," {A} tells the tray. "Let's go again." Half a dose, now, for the other two.
do morale A -3
do trait A warm 2

card p_garden_tend2
type beat
cat life
once
days 21 29
weight 8
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when !flag water_rationed
when !fired water_fail
text {A} waters the last two pods the way you'd check on a sleeping child, and has started reading the seed packet's small print for encouragement. There isn't any. {A} logs that too.
do var garden 1

card p_garden_sprout
type beat
cat wonder
due
once
days 30 37
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when var garden >= 3
text {A} opens the fleet channel and turns the camera on the tray. In the last pod, a pale hook of a shoot has split the seed coat and turned, against no gravity at all, toward the lamp. Six ships go quiet to look.
do morale A 6

card c_garden
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 37 38
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when fired p_garden_sprout
text The entry checklist says loose items go in the locker. {A} reads it, puts the seedling's tray in the locker, and takes it straight back out. Two loops of tape later it is strapped beside the seat. "It rides with me," {A} tells the flight surgeon, who has stopped arguing.
do morale A 3

card p_garden_none
type beat
cat grim
due
once
days 37 37
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when !fired p_garden_sprout
text Rationed water was one squeeze too many: the last pod never came up. {A} keeps watering the tray, two millilitres, on schedule, and packs the dry seed in a coat pocket for the ground. Seeds are patient. So, it turns out, is {A}.
do trait A warm 2

# --- The middle dark ------------------------------------------------------------
card w_venus_shadow
type event
cat wonder
days 10 30
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text With the cabin lights off and the shutters open, {A}'s hand throws a faint shadow on the bulkhead. The light source is Venus. {A} stays there for a long time, moving their fingers, making the planet cast them.
do trait A curious 3

card w_phosphene
type beat
once
cat grim
days 14 28
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} closes their eyes in the bunk and sees a white spark, then another. Cosmic rays, passing straight through the eye, fast enough to make light; cameras see them too, as single bright pixels. {A} counts them like sheep and loses count somewhere in the twenties.
do trait A curious 2
do morale A -1

card w_comet
type event
cat wonder
days 12 30
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text The magnetometer on {A}'s ship twitches for six hours: the fleet is crossing the ion tail of a comet that last came this way before anyone aboard was born. There's nothing to see. {A} sits by the window anyway, with the trace scrolling on a tablet.
do trait A curious 3
do morale A 2

card p_birthday
type beat
cat life
days 7 39
weight 7
once
roles A B
when same A B
text It's {B}'s birthday by the ground calendar, and {A} is aboard for the transfer window. {A} produces a candle that can't be lit, a cake that is a ration bar with a slice of dried mango on it, and a card signed by the whole fleet. {B} keeps the candle.
do bond A B 6
do morale B 5

card p_movie
type beat
cat life
days 7 39
weight 7
once
roles A B
when same A B
text Movie night, with a visitor, on a tablet stuck to the ceiling: {A} picked a film set on a submarine. Halfway through, the hull ticks as the ship turns out of the sun, right on cue. {A} pauses it, and the two of them listen until it stops. Nobody presses play again.
do bond A B 4

card p_dream
type beat
once
cat human
days 10 39
weight 5
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} wakes from a dream of rain on a car roof and lies still, trying to keep the sound. The fans hum. The ship ticks as it turns into the sun. By breakfast the rain has gone, and {A} doesn't mention it to anyone.
do morale A -2
do trait A warm 2

card l_long_table
type event
cat life
days 7 20
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Every seventh flight day the fleet eats together on video: seven tablets on seven galley tables, one meal at one time. {A} is in charge of the toast. It's short, it isn't funny, and it lands.
do morale A 3

card l_long_table2
type event
cat life
days 26 38
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Long table night. {A} has the toast again and gives it to the empty chair at each of the seven tables, the one where a second crew member would sit on a normal ship. It gets a laugh on a short delay from all six screens, and then a quiet.
do morale A 3

card g_third_quarter
type event
cat grim
days 24 34
weight 9
once
roles A B
when cond A ok
when cond B ok
text Past the halfway mark the quiet gets heavier. The flight surgeon calls it the third-quarter effect. On the video link, {A} notices {B} staring at the same page of a checklist for ten minutes, and starts reading the page to {B}, slowly, the way you'd read to a child.
do bond A B 6
do morale B 3

card g_count
type beat
cat grim
days 18 39
weight 5
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} counts the medical kit against the manifest: sutures, splints, a defibrillator with one set of pads. {A} counts it again and closes the lid gently, the way you do when someone is sleeping.
do trait A brave 2

card g_packer
type event
cat human
due
once
days 31 31
roles A
text A batch of photos from the Starbase loading crew reaches {A}: the bay, the cranes, the team in hi-vis. The one with the Sharpie signs off: "Packed every cargo ship since the first. Write when you land. One of them never did."
do morale A 2

card sharpie2
type beat
cat human
days 26 39
weight 12
once
roles A
when fired dil_stash
when cond A ok
text Under the last tray in the spares locker, {A} finds a roll of tape that isn't on any list. Around it, in the same Sharpie hand: "Still thanking me?" Beside it, the little ship again, fingers still crossed. "Every day," {A} tells the empty locker.
do res spares 1
do morale A 5

card p_video_late
type beat
cat human
days 30 36
weight 8
once
roles A
when since t_call >= 25
when !is A ow_list
text A video from home reaches {A} a few minutes after it was sent and a day after the thing it's about. Everyone in it is cheering at something that is already over. {A} cheers back at the screen, alone, on a delay of their own.
do morale A 2

# --- The approach --------------------------------------------------------------
card w_aurora
type event
cat arrival
days 33 39
weight 9
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text In one of the orbiters' night frames {A} finds a faint green smear over dark ground: Martian aurora, patchy, pinned to old magnetized rock nobody has ever touched. {A} saves the frame, then sits with it on the screen a while longer than the job needs.
do trait A curious 3

card w_phobos
type event
cat arrival
days 40 40
weight 14
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Phobos is a speck beside Mars now, crossing its face in under an hour. {A} watches it cross a whole world in the time it takes to eat a meal, and can't remember the last time they wanted to stand on something this badly.
do trait A curious 2
do morale A 3

card w_mars_disc
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag c2_answered
when !is A ow_hail
text On the last night before entry, {A} holds a thumb up to the window, the old habit from the Earth watches. For forty days everything has fitted behind it. Now Mars spills out around it on every side, rust and dark, and somewhere on the night side, too small to see, a light is holding steady.
do morale A 5

card w_mars_disc_q
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when !flag c2_answered
when !is A ow_hail
text On the last night before entry, {A} holds a thumb up to the window, the old habit from the Earth watches. For forty days everything has fitted behind it. Now Mars spills out around it on every side, rust and dark, and somewhere on the night side, too small to see, a light is keeping time.
do morale A 5

card a_last_night
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A B
when is A ow_dose
text The last night before entry. {A} checks the water tanks that shielded the bunk all these weeks, by hand, the way you'd pat a horse. On the fleet channel {B} is doing the same on another ship. "Same time tomorrow?" {B} asks. "On the ground," {A} says. Neither of them sleeps much.
do bond A B 6

# --- Arrival day: what the fleet chose, and what it cost ------------------------------
card a_recall_home
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag name_home
text On the entry map {A} finds the crater the fleet named for a small town at home, right where it should be. Cargo 2 has been standing behind its rim the whole time. Somewhere on Earth, a town newspaper is about to need a second front page.

card a_recall_plan
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag name_plan
text On the entry map {A} finds the crater the fleet named for the first person who ever wrote a Mars plan. Cargo 2 has been standing behind its rim the whole time. Somewhere on Earth, a committee is about to have a great deal more to argue about.

card a_recall_photo
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag photo_taken
text {A} stows the tablet with the fleet portrait on it: seven ships, Earth behind them, and the propellant it took to fly them that close, which would have been nice to have today. Worth it, {A} decides, and means it.

card a_recall_wrist
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when fired crisis_eva
when is A eva_who
text {A} straps in for entry with the wrist that wouldn't bend, mostly bending now, and doesn't mention the "mostly" to the flight surgeon.

card a_recall_valve
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag valve_out
when is A valve_who
text Entry on {A}'s ship runs one thruster short. The valve isolated that night has stayed shut ever since, and the entry sequence was rewritten around it weeks ago. {A} reads the workaround once more and initials it.

card a_recall_stash
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag stash_shared
when !fired a_recall_wrist
when is A stash_who
text On the morning of entry {A} unpins the empty ration bag from the galley wall and folds it into a pocket, Sharpie side out.

card a_recall_shared
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A B
when flag stash_exposed
when is A stash_who
when !fired a_recall_wrist
text Before strapping in, {A} sends {B} the last pack from the locker on the morning transfer, with a note on the bag in borrowed handwriting: "You'll thank me."
do bond B A 3

card a_recall_hail
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when !fired a_recall_wrist
when !fired a_recall_stash
when is A ow_hail
text The standing hail is still in the comms schedule, one line, weeks old. {A} takes it out by hand, and the big dish turns back to Earth for good, with the letters that waited behind it.

card a_recall_quiet
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when !fired a_recall_wrist
when !fired a_recall_stash
when is A ow_hail
text The big dish never turned away from Earth, and every letter from home arrived on time. {A} answers the last one on the morning of entry and adds a line nobody at home will understand yet: "We're going to say hello in person."
